# Design Patterns lab style

This repo is coursework for **Design Patterns**. Prefer classic OOP patterns and clear layers over clever shortcuts.

## Layering (required)

| Layer | Responsibility | Must NOT |
|-------|----------------|----------|
| `entities/` | Data only (`id`, points, getters) | Compute area/volume, validate files, log |
| `factories/` | Create entities from raw input (Factory Method) | Business formulas |
| `validators/` | Input + calculation checks | Create entities, own geometry formulas beyond checks |
| `services/` | Business logic (area, type checks, splits) | Parse files, hold I/O |
| `io/` | Read paths safely | Know shape math |
| `exceptions/` | Domain errors (extend app base) | Throw bare `Error` for domain cases |

## Patterns to use when fitting

- **Factory Method**: abstract `ShapeFactory` + concrete factories per figure; `createFromLine` returns entity or skips invalid input.
- **Template / shared base**: `Shape` with `id` + `getPoints()`; figures extend it.
- Prefer composition (inject Geometry, validators into services) over static utility bags.
- One reason to change per class (SRP). Do not dump triangle + pyramid logic into one god service.

## Geometry / Point modeling

- A single `Point(x, y, z = 0)` for 2D and 3D is acceptable when variants mix planes and space: 2D figures live on `z = 0`.
- Do not invent `Point2D`/`Point3D` unless the assignment explicitly requires separate types or LSP is broken in practice.
- Keep figures axis-aligned / parallel to coordinate planes when the brief says so — simplifies volume splits and defense.

## Input, errors, logging

- Read from project-relative `.txt` only; reject paths outside the project.
- Invalid lines: validate → custom exception → catch in factory → log warn → continue (do not crash the run).
- Never throw-and-immediately-catch in the same block; catch at the boundary that can recover.
- Log with `pino` to console and file.

## Tests

- Jest (or Mocha): multiple expects per case; mix matchers (`toBe`, `toBeCloseTo`, `toThrow`, `toBeInstanceOf`).
- Cover valid figures, invalid file lines, and calculation validators.

## When changing code

- Prefer deleting dead abstraction over adding new pattern “for show”.
- If both 2D and 3D variants exist, share `Point`/`Shape`/`Geometry`; keep figure-specific code in its factory/validator/service.
- Name immutable constants `UPPER_SNAKE`; keep regexes in `constants/`.
---

## Defense one-liners (if user asks)

- Entity vs Service: “данные отдельно, формулы в service — требование entity без бизнес-логики”.
- Factory Method: “клиент зовёт `createFromLine`, конкретный тип создаёт наследник фабрики”.
- Point 3D for triangle: “одна модель точки в пространстве; треугольник — сечение z=0”.
